					Title: <b>Dang Fabled and being KSed</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Inobu</b> on <b>March 28, 2005, 06:55:19 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Was camping Fabled Eldak to get ring for a couple of guildies. He popped but healer had to go, so i log on a friends Sk to tank him while 3 guildies held camp. Just to zone in and find out that he was KSed =/<br /><br />Hope Hunnibuns,Necras and Naturesangel get kicked out of the fine Guild League of Sozobon, which o know there are many nice people in there =/</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Dang Fabled and being KSed</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Naithein</b> on <b>March 28, 2005, 11:22:08 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Hum...Where you engaged with the mob before htey starting fighting? Because if you weren&#039;t then theres no KSing there.<br /><br />Could get them for disrespecting camps, but SoE doesn&#039;t recognize those anyway.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Dang Fabled and being KSed</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Self Destruction</b> on <b>March 29, 2005, 05:44:53 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">So what&#039;s the minimum amount of time one should wait for a camp while there&#039;s another group there who&#039;s not attempting or capable of holding it on their own?</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Dang Fabled and being KSed</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Moraganna</b> on <b>March 29, 2005, 08:50:51 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Forevah!!&nbsp;  :)</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Dang Fabled and being KSed</b><br />
					Post by: <b>EQSysquella</b> on <b>March 29, 2005, 02:20:08 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><b>group_01_without_force_to_kill</b> sobs<br /><br />Time (in seconds) = Desireability * Spawn Time / Patience<br /><br />We will base desireability on a 1-10pt scale.&nbsp; 1 being high, 10 being low.&nbsp; <br />spawn time will be based on a 1-10pt scale.&nbsp; 10 being a short spawn time, and 1 being a LONG spawn time.<br />Patience is based on a 1-3pt scale.&nbsp; 1= patient.&nbsp; 2= patient enough.&nbsp; 3= impatient.<br /><br />So if you have a HIGH desireability of 1 on a 1-pt long spawn time with a patience level of 3.. <br /><br />Time = 1*1/3 = .33seconds (roughly translated to as soon as they are in range to fire an arrow or cast a spell)<br /><br />Now lets look at a different scenario.. with Desireability being 10 and spawn time being 10 with a patience level of 1.<br /><br />TIme = 10*10/1 = 1min 40seconds.&nbsp; (which is a lot to ask for)<br /><br />___________________________<br /><br />anyone who actually read that-- I am sorry for taking 5minutes of your life.&nbsp; </div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
