					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Dang Fabled and being KSed</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Hunnibun Sammich</b> on <b>April 15, 2005, 08:07:52 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Ok to bring us all back to the original post:<br /><br />1.&nbsp; They were not engaged.<br /><br />2.&nbsp; I engaged and the mob was following me to my group and <br />&nbsp; &nbsp;  they attacked it after i had engaged it.<br /><br />3.&nbsp; They were not ready to engage they were waiting for an<br />&nbsp; &nbsp;  sk to take out the mob because their cleric bailed.<br /><br />So it would be safe to say we did not ks from them, if anything they tried to ks us but were unsucessful.<br /><br /> :wiggle:</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Dang Fabled and being KSed</b><br />
					Post by: <b>twichythumb</b> on <b>April 15, 2005, 12:43:16 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I used to roam around BoT with my roommate&#039;s cleric Bendan and kill off ornate dropping names for tormenter stir fry funds, twink funds, and casino money. Now, being a crappy low dps hybrid and all, my KS rules were pretty simple: If you can&#039;t kill it faster than me and my greenie pet, it&#039;s mine. It takes me around 7 minutes to clear a named room and 4-8 minutes to take out a named (depending on which one it is)... while my roomate yawns, watches anime on the side, and proves that YES, clerics CAN be a one button class! So you see, if you can&#039;t beat me out at my sloth&#039;s pace clearing, you wouldn&#039;t have been able to kill it anyway... you&#039;re too... how should I put this... sunk in mediocrity. If, on the other hand, you and your motely crew steamroll past my 2 man team and pound the named into so many unrecognizable bits before my very eyes, more power to you. I don&#039;t comlain. You&#039;ve proven your worth in my eyes and I&#039;ll go pick on some other, more pathetic group.<br /><br />Likewise, if your group up and croaks on some named at 10-17% while I&#039;m galloping around aimlessly, it&#039;s fair game to me... I&#039;ll just HT it and put it out of its misery (and relieve it of its loot). Don&#039;t complain. I extended the courtesy of letting you commit collective sepeku first.<br /><br />As for fabled... yes, I recognize the fact that certain &quot;big burst burn&quot; classes can basically KS them at will with the click of a button. Personally, I usually didn&#039;t. Their loot are mostly twink toys, and I think it&#039;s poor form to begrudge some pathetic noob of his &quot;holy grail&quot;, which I on the other hand, would stick on a twink I play once every blue moon. If, on the other hand, it&#039;s dead obvious that the loot&#039;s going to YOUR twink... well... I&#039;d have to say that my twink takes precedence. Don&#039;t whine. Just because you CAN&#039;T KS, doesn&#039;t mean other people WON&#039;T.<br /><br />Anyone remember the &quot;good old days&quot; when ppl farmed rathe mountains hill giants for plat and really crappy exp? Anyone develop a keen dislike for druids and necros because they took all the kills? Same deal. Don&#039;t complain. Just cause we CAN&#039;T druidwhack mobs and SOW ourselves to run faster than the competition doesn&#039;t mean they shouldn&#039;t.<br /><br />Having said all this, I&#039;m not a complete ass (except on occasion when the mood strikes me). It pays to be civil to your neighbors, and in the everquest community, a little consideration usually goes a long way. Those who knew me would probably attest that I DIDN&#039;T KS ppl... not because I couldn&#039;t... but because, barring exceptional circumstances (like a group trying to take out a mob they just reasonably can&#039;t or a group taking forever to take out a mob) it&#039;s just a dastardly thing to do. And really, it&#039;s just not worth becoming public enemy #1 just to get some marginally useful toy. Remember, Norrath&#039;s a big world, and most little fish have at least a few big bad friends. Eventually, most actions come back to roost in some form or another, and it just might be YOUR group or raid that get&#039;s steamrolled the next time a mob pops.<br /><br />So what&#039;s the point of all this rambling? I guess, to put is simply... it&#039;s good to get along... shit happens sometimes... deal with it and stop bitching. That&#039;s all&nbsp; :)</div>
					<br />
